In article <1993Oct17.055334.23608@bsu-ucs>, 01mbmccabe@leo.bsuvc.bsu.edu writes:
|> Does anyone know how to use the "! - Escape to shell" option in NetHack 3.1.3
|> with Gemini/Mupfel on an Atari Mega ST4?
|> 
|> I tried executing NETHACK.TOS from the Mupfel CLI and the "!"'ing in NetHack
|> but got a message to the effect the C:\Gemini\Mupfel.APP could not be ececuted.

Strange. I also play nethack on my Mega ST4, and escaping to Mupfel works
fine. Are you sure you didn't load nethack with the Gemini/Mupfel "overload"
option? This memory-saving feature always deletes Gemini resp. Mupfel from the 
memory before loading nethack and reloads it afterwards.

